  "history": {
    "origins": "Zwicker (Zwickern) is a North German fishing game from Schleswig-Holstein, related to Casino and Scopa. First recorded in print in 1930 in Robert Hülsemann's Das Buch der Spiele; originally played with a 52-card pack, now commonly with 3, 4, or 6 jokers. Popular in Dithmarschen, North Frisia, and Eiderstedt; 58-card Zwicker packs were sold from the 1950s by ASS and Nürnberger Spielkarten.",
    "originCountries": ["Germany"],
    "timeline": ["20th century: North German fishing game from Schleswig-Holstein; Zwicker cards sold from 1950s (ASS, Nürnberger Spielkarten)."],
    "evolution": "Related to Casino/Scopa family.",
    "cultural": "Schleswig-Holstein regional tradition.",
    "hasPlaceholders": false
  },
